review_text:
Beautiful tactical.

Pros :

- kill stuff (well, mostly guards) in a beautiful Edo-era Japan ;
- various array of tactics to take down your enemies, with challenging situations (you probably won't be bored with that one);
- each character has a great personality, which adds even more flavor to a nice storyline ;
- to be a ninja or a kunoichi really feels good in this game.

Cons :

- you will scratch your head more than once with this one. Prepare to die a lot, and retry a lot to fully handle what you have to do ;
- if you want to unlock everything, arm yourself with patience, for you will retry stuff over and over and over....

Time to scarper... this samurai is getting suspicious of me.

[b]Is it nice?[/b] [i]Yeah, pretty neat pixellated graphics[/i];
[b]Does it sound good?[/b] [i]Meh, the soundtrack is ok but nothing great[/i];
[b]Does it run smoothly?[/b] [i]Absolutely, even on the potatoest pc[/i];
[b]Is it easy?[/b] [i]No, it's unjustifiably hard and unforgiving[/i];
[b]Is it fun?[/b] [i]For the most part, it's also kind of repetitive[/i].

Buy it on discount, you might get bored sooner than you think, but it's worth a try,

[b] ENGLISH  [/b]
This is a game similar to what happened with CS, they made another one to try to improve it but you can't see anything exciting that makes you say "this game is absolutely different from its predecessor". Don't take this the wrong way, but this game is full of bugs and long loading times. In addition to being poorly optimized, unlike boneworks which had plenty of fps running with good graphics, here running on a good machine with graphics at least it causes some bottlenecks sometimes for no reason at all! But even with these problems, I finished the game and enjoyed it! 
[b] OPTIMIZATION TIPS [/b]
[list]
If you want to play the game anyway:
[*] Optimize your PC by closing unused applications on your PC;
[*] If you use programs to set animated wallpapers, make the taskbar transparent, etc., CLOSE these applications, they may seem like they don't consume anything, but they use A LOT of memory;
[*] Remove animations from windows;
[*] Place in "Power Options" under High Performance;
[*] Cleaning temporary files by clicking WIN + R or searching for "Run" in the Windows search and entering %temp% and temp, see if you won't lose anything important and delete everything from the folder *depending on it, you can free up gigabytes of these folders*; 
[*] Now going to graphics configuration/graphics performance preference click on browse and find the BoneLab folder and click on the bonelab .exe and set it to high performance;
[*] Go to the library and locate the game and go to Properties and put this command "-vrmode oculus" in the launch options, if you are a Meta quest user;
[/list]

[b] PORTUGUÊS [/b]
Esse é um jogo parecido com o que houve com cs, fizeram outro para tentar melhorar mas não da de ver nada de empolgante que você fale "esse jogo é absolutamente diferente do seu antecessor". Não levem a mal mas esse jogo está repleto de bugs e loadings demorados. Além de estar mal otimizado, diferente de boneworks que sobrava fps rodando com gráfico bom , aqui rodando em uma máquina boa com os gráficos no mínimo da uns gargalos as vezes por questão nenhuma! Mas mesmo com esses poréns zerei o jogo e gostei ! 
[b] DICAS de OTIMIZAÇÃO [/b]
[list]
Caso queira jogar o jogo mesmo assim:
[*] Otimize seu pc fechando aplicativos sem uso no pc;
[*] Se você utiliza programas para colocar wallpapers animados, deixar a barra de tarefas transparentes , etc, FECHE esse aplicativos até podem parecer que não consomem nada mas eles utilizam BASTANTE memória;
[*] Tirar animações do windows;
[*] Colocar em "Opções de Energia" em Alto Desempenho;
[*] Limpando arquivos temporários clicando WIN + R ou pesquisando "Executar" na busca do windows e colocar %temp% e temp veja se não irá perder nada de importante e apague tudo da pasta *dependendo pode liberar gigas destas pastas*; 
[*] Agora indo em configuração de elementos gráficos/ preferência de desempenho de gráficos clique em procurar e encontre a pasta do BoneLab e clique no .exe do bonelab e coloque como alto desempenho;
[*] Vá na biblioteca e localize o jogo e vá em Propriedades e coloque em opções de inicialização esse comando "-vrmode oculus" , caso você seja usuário do Meta quest ;
[/list]

enjoy story? like smashing buttons and pretty lights? like seriously how adhd are you? if you answered yes to any of these you should give sword art online fractured daydream a try. description with three epic multiplayer modes its hard to pin down think fortnite versus monsters pitting teams against on another to score higher.

you unlock modes by doing story until you get co op quests.  think of the story as the tutorial it brings you into gameplay mechanics through story. personally i love this part. as you progress through the story you unlock more characters to play. if you really need to you can skip most cutscenes. WHY other than time would you want to?  

honestley really great game not for everyone however its a great melding of game genres. waaay go peoples yall have made a great game. hands down looking forward to raise my ranks. :}

Overall not my favourite Yakuza experience, but I still enjoyed it.

Here are my highlights:
- Dragon Spirit;
- The game now includes side stories on top of substories. I liked most of them, and the substories are still pleasant;
- Haruka's story and gameplay will be a hit of miss, but I enjoyed them;
- I did like how all stories tied together;
- I liked how you could choose who to play as during the later chapters;
- The speeches about dreams.

Here are the things I enjoyed a bit less:
- I thought the story was overextending its welcome, especially by the end (although this could also be me blazing through every Yakuza game so fast);
- Shinada. I like the character, but I found that by the time he is introduced, it was hard to yet again "restart" another story (even if I knew it'd
eventually become intertwined with the main story). By that point, you've already played as 4 characters and the story is well-established, with several hooks;
- With so many characters, some gameplay is bound to be less interesting to you, and I found that to be Shinada's case (I liked his fighting style less).

Person sitting on a bench floating above a table;
an innkeeper leaning on the table while the innkeeper cleans, and both of them passing through each other's bodies;
wagons that don't stop when you're standing on the road and push you aside even when you're on your horse;
items that respawn even though you've already picked them up;
villagers who can't pass when there's a wagon in the middle of the road and keep bumping into it;
no one bothers to look back to see what you're doing behind them or if they'll be robbed;
characters who stand in the same place for too long day after day, such as at the camp;
Cumans, after interactions, stand in the same place day after day;
sword combos are impossible to perform using a computer mouse;
you can stand over people sleeping and they don't mind;
phrases repeated too frequently while you roll dice;
Henry made a big deal with cutscenes and emotion about losing his dog and finding his horse was no big deal, that was stupid...

I just arrived in Kuttenberg so there are probably still a lot of bugs that I will report.
